.\" Man page for magicdl. PUBLIC DOMAIN (CC0-1.0)
.TH MAGICDL 1 "@DATE@" "magicdl @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
magicdl \- index, download, and organize purchased digital collections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magicdl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B magicdl
keeps a local index of the content you own on supported stores, downloads what
is new, and verifies what is already on disk. It tracks multiple versions of an
item, records removed, hidden, and pre-ordered content, and stores a SHA\-256
per downloaded file so moved files can be relocated and integrity checked.
.PP
A run selects a backend with
.B \-\-backend
and supplies that backend's credentials. The state lives in a SQLite index
named by
.BR \-\-db .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list\-backends
List the available backends.
.TP
.B index
Fetch the list of owned content and store it, without downloading files.
.TP
.BI "sync " "[id...]"
Download content. With no arguments it lists the whole collection from the
store and downloads what is new. With item ids it resolves only those from the
index. With
.B \-\-from\-index
it downloads what is already indexed without contacting the store's listing,
narrowed by the list filters (for example
.BR \-\-not\-downloaded ).
.TP
.B verify
Check downloaded files. Mark each present or missing;
.B \-\-rehash
re\-hashes present files to detect changed content;
.B \-\-rescan
hashes the output tree and relocates files that were moved, matched by hash.
.TP
.B status
Show a summary of the collection: item and version counts, per\-format and
per\-backend breakdowns, and total size.
.TP
.B list
List items, one per line, with filters such as
.BR \-\-status ", " \-\-not\-downloaded ", and " \-\-limit .
.TP
.BI "details " id
Show one item's versions and the files under each.
.TP
.BI "blacklist " "id..."
Mark items so
.B sync
skips them. Add
.B \-\-reason
to note why.
.TP
.BI "allow " "id..."
Remove items from the blacklist.
.TP
.BI "relocate " "old new"
Record that an item moved from one id to another. The old item is skipped by
.BR sync .
.TP
.BI "import " dir
Mark indexed items that already exist under an
.IR Artist / "YYYY \- Album"
music library so
.B sync
skips them. Matching is by name. Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to review matches before marking.
.TP
.B manifest
Write a browsable library manifest, one section per backend, in Markdown
(default) or HTML with
.BR \-\-html .
Each item is a checkbox, ticked when the index records it as downloaded, so run
.B verify
first for an accurate picture.
.B \-\-no\-check
lists items without checkboxes.
.B \-\-out\-file
writes to a file instead of standard output (an
.B .html
extension selects HTML). The list filters scope the manifest.
.TP
.BI "key " "set|get|rm"
Manage a backend's key in the system keyring; needs
.BR \-\-backend ,
and an optional
.B \-\-user
to keep several accounts of one backend apart (the plain form is the default
account, a named one is used only when the same
.B \-\-user
is given to
.B index
or
.BR sync ).
.B set
reads a key from the terminal without echoing it (or from standard input when
piped) and stores it;
.B get
prints the stored key;
.B rm
removes it. Once a key is stored, commands read it from the keyring
automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Selection and credentials
.TP
.BI "\-\-backend " name
Backend to use (see
.BR BACKENDS ).
.TP
.BI "\-\-user " name
The Bandcamp fan\-page handle, and the keyring account to use (see
.BR key );
the plain form, with no
.BR \-\-user ,
is the default account.
.TP
.BI "\-\-scope " ref
Restrict
.B index
or
.B sync
to a subset of the collection named by
.IR ref ,
instead of the whole collection. The reference is backend specific: for itch.io
it is a bundle link
.RB ( https://itch.io/b/ \fIid\fR / \fIslug\fR ", or the numeric " id ),
and only items you own from that bundle are listed. A scoped
.B index
does not sweep, so it will not mark the rest of your library removed. A backend
that does not support scoping reports so. A resolved scope is cached under
.I <data dir>/cache
for a day and reused;
.B \-\-refresh
ignores the cache and re\-fetches.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Ignore any cached
.B \-\-scope
result and resolve it again from the network.
.TP
.BI "\-\-app\-key " key
Application or API key (DriveThruRPG, itch.io). Exposes the key in the process
list; prefer the keyring or the file form.
.TP
.BI "\-\-app\-key\-file " path
Read the application or API key from a file, so it never appears on the command
line.
.TP
.BI "\-\-cookies " path
Cookies file (Bandcamp): a Firefox cookies.sqlite, a Cookie Quick Manager JSON
export, or a Netscape cookies.txt.
.TP
.B \-\-firefox
Load Bandcamp cookies from the Firefox profiles on this machine.
.SS Storage and content
.TP
.BI "\-\-db " path
Index database. Defaults to the config
.B db
key, or
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/magicdl.sqlite
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/magicdl/
when that variable is set).
.TP
.BI "\-\-out " dir
Output directory. Required; taken from the config
.B out
key when not given. There is no built\-in default.
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " list
Content formats, comma\-separated. For a single\-file backend (Bandcamp) the
first entry is the audio format to request
.RB ( flac ", " vorbis " for ogg, " mp3\-320 ", ...)."
For multi\-file backends the list keeps only those file types (for example
.BR pdf ", " pdf,epub ).
Unset means
.B flac
for Bandcamp and every file elsewhere.
.TP
.B \-\-covers
Also download cover images (Bandcamp).
.TP
.B \-\-from\-index
For
.BR sync :
download from the stored index without listing from the store.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-hidden
Skip hidden collection items when indexing.
.SS verify
.TP
.B \-\-rehash
Re\-hash present files to check integrity.
.TP
.B \-\-rescan
Relocate moved files by content hash, scanning
.BR \-\-out .
.SS list filters
.TP
.BI "\-\-status " s
Only items with this status
.RB ( active ", " removed ", " preorder ", " unavailable ).
.TP
.B \-\-hidden ", " \-\-blacklisted ", " \-\-superseded
Only items with the named flag.
.TP
.B \-\-downloaded ", " \-\-not\-downloaded
Only items that are, or are not, downloaded.
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " n
Cap the number of items.
.SS manifest
.TP
.BI "\-\-out\-file " path
Write the manifest to this file instead of standard output. An
.B .html
extension selects HTML output.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Write the manifest as HTML rather than Markdown.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-check
Omit the download checkboxes and the download tally.
.SS Output and pacing
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output for
.BR status ", " list ", " details ", " verify ", " blacklist ", " allow ", and " relocate .
.TP
.BI "\-\-interval\-ms " n
Base delay between requests. Default 3000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-retries " n
Retries per request. Default 5.
.TP
.BI "\-\-timeout\-ms " n
Per\-request timeout. Default 30000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-reason " text
Note why an item is blacklisted.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and report without writing files.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B bandcamp
Audio. Authenticates with browser cookies
.RB ( \-\-firefox " or " \-\-cookies )
and needs
.BR \-\-user .
.TP
.B drivethrurpg
RPG PDFs and files. Authenticates with an application key from the account's
"Library App Keys" page.
.TP
.B itchio
Games, tools, and assets. Authenticates with an API key from
itch.io/user/settings/api\-keys. Downloads mirror the store layout,
.IR <user> .itch.io/ <slug> ,
taken from each item's page URL, rather than the default
.IR Creator " - " Title
folder.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Bandcamp uses your logged\-in browser session cookies. DriveThruRPG and itch.io
use an application or API key.
.PP
The preferred store for a key is the system keyring, the freedesktop Secret
Service served by GNOME Keyring or KWallet, reached through
.B libsecret
loaded at run time. Store a key with
.RB "\[dq]" "magicdl key set \-\-backend " name "\[dq]"
and later commands read it automatically. When no keyring is available, keep
the key in a file readable only by you and pass
.B \-\-app\-key\-file
so the secret does not appear in the process list.
.PP
A key is resolved in this order, first match wins:
.BR \-\-app\-key ,
then
.B \-\-app\-key\-file
or the config
.BR app\-key\-file ,
then the keyring, then a bare
.B app\-key
in the config. A configured key file therefore overrides the keyring.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/magicdl/config.ini
Optional config file
.RB ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magicdl/config.ini
when that variable is set). A
.B [general]
section and a
.BI [backend. name ]
section per backend set defaults for
.BR db ", " out ", " user ", " app\-key\-file ", " cookies ", and " format .
A backend section overrides
.BR [general] ,
and a command\-line option overrides both. Paths may use
.B ~
and environment variables.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/magicdl.sqlite
Default index database
.RB ( $XDG_DATA_HOME/magicdl/
when set; override with
.B \-\-db
or the config
.B db
key). The index is a rebuildable cache and holds no secrets. If it is corrupted
and will not open, delete it together with any
.BR \-journal ", " \-wal ", or " \-shm
sidecar file next to it
.RB ( "rm magicdl.sqlite*" )
and run
.B index
again to rebuild it; downloaded files are untouched.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/magicdl/cache/
Cached
.B \-\-scope
resolutions, reused for a day. Safe to delete;
.B \-\-refresh
also rewrites them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Index a DriveThruRPG library:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl index \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey
.EE
.RE
.PP
Download everything not yet fetched, from the index, without re\-listing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey \-\-out ~/rpg \-\-from\-index \-\-not\-downloaded
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fetch only the PDFs of an item:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend drivethrurpg \-\-app\-key\-file .appkey \-\-out ~/rpg \-\-format pdf 12345
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sync a Bandcamp collection as ogg:
.PP
.RS
.EX
magicdl sync \-\-backend bandcamp \-\-user yourhandle \-\-firefox \-\-out ~/music \-\-format vorbis
.EE
.RE
.SH RATE LIMITING
Some stores are quick to rate limit and slow to forgive. Requests are spaced out
and backed off after an HTTP 429. The defaults are conservative;
.B \-\-interval\-ms
sets a faster base pace when an account tolerates it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B magicdl
exits 0 on success, 1 on an error, and 2 on an unknown command.
.SH COPYRIGHT
PUBLIC DOMAIN (CC0\-1.0).
